  "section_notes": "The final S2 keeps the 5% level but makes sales suspension after a failed verified retest a regulator decision rather than automatic, so the Hearth 10 (6.2%) is not forced off the market, and this is the most significant weakening. S3 sets a 6-year retrofit deadline, which favours Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage, while S5 keeps the mandatory 8-per-100,000 recall trigger that would reach Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9). S1 reporting is strong (24-hour reporting for all thermal incidents), and S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months, which is within the acceptable range."
